# The two files packed into the Windows zip are shipped to readers exactly as
# they are written: UTF-8 with a BOM and CRLF line endings, which is what
# Notepad needs to show Arabic, and to show line breaks at all. No end-of-line
# conversion in either direction, on any machine that checks them out —
# including the runner that packs them.
#
# The rule lives here rather than in that directory because the packaging step
# copies everything in it into the zip, and a .gitattributes is not something
# anyone downloaded the app to read.
.github/windows-package/* -text
